1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,633
Wait! Hold it…!

2
00:00:02,633 --> 00:00:04,700
How can you close it on someone?!

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:06,300
Dad, someone's running over.

4
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,433
They can take the next one. So what~

5
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:12,533
When I do it, so what. When you do it, illegal. Double standard, number one.

6
00:00:12,533 --> 00:00:15,767
I'm… Modapman.

7
00:00:17,567 --> 00:00:20,933
Case summary. Saturday morning, 15th floor.

8
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:22,967
Behave in the elevator today.

9
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:25,700
Who has better manners than me?

10
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,633
There are. Three hundred in this building alone.

11
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:31,467
Just three rounds. Round one: the close button.

12
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:33,767
You pressed close too, just now.

13
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:36,167
I pressed it because I was busy,

14
00:00:36,167 --> 00:00:38,900
he did it because he's impatient.

15
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:40,967
Double standard, number two.

16
00:00:40,967 --> 00:00:43,700
This is called the actor-observer bias.

17
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:45,300
Actor… what?

18
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,700
Press it ten times, it counts as once.

19
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:49,200
…How long have you been there?

20
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:51,467
But mashing it makes it faster!

21
00:00:51,467 --> 00:00:53,933
Many are built not to close right away.

22
00:00:53,933 --> 00:00:56,500
For whoever's behind you, it's the open button.

23
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:56,833
…Huh?

24
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:58,633
Round two: the floor buttons.

25
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:02,433
14, 13, 12… every single floor?!

26
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:04,333
Where are the parents?!

27
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:05,167
That afternoon.

28
00:01:05,167 --> 00:01:07,600
Honey, why'd you press 5 and 6?

29
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:10,067
Just a mistake~ So what.

30
00:01:10,067 --> 00:01:11,633
Double standard, number three.

31
00:01:11,633 --> 00:01:15,200
Mistake or prank, it stops at every floor you press.

32
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,033
…Looks like you're "the parents" now.

33
00:01:18,033 --> 00:01:19,800
Round three: phone calls.

34
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:24,067
Talking that loud in here? So rude.

35
00:01:24,067 --> 00:01:25,400
Your voice is loud too.

36
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:27,467
Yes, sir! I'll put you on speaker!

37
00:01:27,467 --> 00:01:29,467
It's an urgent call. So what~

38
00:01:29,467 --> 00:01:30,933
Double standard, number four.

39
00:01:30,933 --> 00:01:33,333
In this box, everyone hears everything.

40
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:35,167
Take the call after you get off.

41
00:01:35,167 --> 00:01:35,633
…Huh?

42
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:39,300
Dad, the close button, the buttons, the call…

43
00:01:39,367 --> 00:01:42,300
You see it when others do it, but not when you do?

44
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:45,167
…Yeah. I couldn't see myself.

45
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:47,800
The one running over is someone's dad too.

46
00:01:47,933 --> 00:01:49,700
I'm late, I'm late!

47
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,100
Dad, someone's running!

48
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:52,133
HONEY!!

49
00:01:52,133 --> 00:01:56,367
That's not a double standard. She's not a stranger, she's his wife. Just a wrong answer.

50
00:01:56,367 --> 00:01:59,300
15th floor. One wife left behind.

51
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,500
…Classic Modapman.
